      "message": "This copy is inside the test body after step_run_restperfclient, so when restperfclient itself fails or times out the test raises first and the log never reaches results/ — leaving it only in tmp/, which the next run wipes. That is the failure whose log is most worth keeping. Could this move to an unconditional teardown (or a try/finally)? If the placement is deliberate, the comment\u0027s \"always-executed test case\" claim should be softened, since only a check failure is covered.",
